  "evidence": "TEXT_D backs ECHR incorporation, a Human Rights Commission, devolution and proportional representation, non‑discriminatory immigration and restored asylum support, LGBT equality (equal age of consent, repeal Section 28, anti‑discrimination), robust environmentalism (carbon tax, major CO2 cuts, renewables), and deeper EU engagement. TEXT_G frames EU integration as a transfer of powers to supranational institutions, urges a referendum on whether to join a federal Europe or revert to an association of sovereign nations, and stresses restoring/maintaining national sovereignty.",
  "reasoning": "TEXT_D argues from social liberalisation, civil rights, multiculturalism, and internationalism, placing it on the GAL side. TEXT_G argues from national sovereignty over supranational authority, aligning with TAN priorities, so it better matches a TAN‑leaning electorate.",
